# Walkthrough: Phase 1 — Memory Agent & Context Window Expansion

All components for **Phase 1** have been implemented, tested, and verified.

## 1. What Was Implemented

### A. Autonomous Memory Agent (`backend/memory_agent.py`)
- Created `MemoryAgent` with a sliding window threshold of 6 turns.
- When history exceeds 6 turns, `MemoryAgent.compress()` sends turns `1..N-2` to GLM-4.7-Flash with `MEMORY_COMPRESSION_PROMPT`.
- Replaces raw turns with a 2-3 sentence executive `[Session Memory Summary: ...]` system passage, preserving the most recent 2 turns verbatim.

### B. Route Integration (`backend/routes.py`)
- Imported `MemoryAgent` and added `history = MemoryAgent.compress(raw_history)` at the top of the `/chat` route.
- Ensured automatic Zoho OAuth token refresh via `Config.refresh_access_token()` when token expiry (10-minute window) is encountered.

### C. Frontend Clean History Payload (`Chatbot.jsx`)
- Expanded history payload window from 5 to **8 turns** (`.slice(-8)`).
- Filtered out welcome message (`id !== 'welcome'`).
- Stripped all HTML tags (`<br>`, `<b>`, `<span>`) from bot responses before forwarding history to backend.

